From dd0ffa9838faafaf8b8aaf5a0e45622d0102ba80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:17:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: OPLUS: a request the firmware
 rejects is an error

The reply to an OnePlus request (opcodes 0x300 set / 0x301 get) was taken
as a success whatever its result word said; only the value was stored.
These requests are the input current limit, charge enable and the 9 V
request. A write of inhibit-charge to charge_behaviour therefore returned
success even if the firmware had refused it, and "charger setup ...
failed" could only fire on a transport error or a timeout.

The vendor's driver checks the result word of every reply, also for these
opcodes (validate_message(): ret_code != 0 is an error).

Return -EIO for a result other than 0 and log the firmware's code once
per property.

Tested on the OnePlus Pad 4: every SET and GET of the charger setup
answers result 0, no "rejected" line, the charger line and the inhibit
behave as before.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index c39a5d97b1..cf2b0d12a6 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -2076,6 +2076,14 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_sm8350_callback(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 	case OPLUS_PROPERTY_SET:
 	case OPLUS_PROPERTY_GET:
 		battmgr->oplus_value = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+		/* stock: a reply with a result word other than 0 is an error (validate_message) */
+		if (payload_len == sizeof(resp->intval) && resp->intval.result) {
+			dev_warn_ratelimited(battmgr->dev,
+					     "request %#x property %u rejected by the charger firmware: %u\n",
+					     opcode, le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.property),
+					     le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.result));
+			battmgr->error = -EIO;
+		}
 		break;
 	default:
 		dev_warn(battmgr->dev, "unknown message %#x\n", opcode);
-- 
